[[File:Ice_Barrage.gif|thumb|400px|A [[Player character|player]] using [[Ice Barrage]] against another player, Freezing them and thus preventing movement]]

'''Freeze''', also referred to as [[Bind]], [[Entangle]] or '''Root''' is a [[Status effect]] which restricts movement of affected players and NPCs, rendering them immobile for a period of time without disabling other actions. Due to the specialised nature of Freezes (i.e., restricting only movement) they usually last significantly longer than [[Stun (status)|Stuns]].

== Mechanics ==
'''Freeze''' restricts [[Game square|movement]] for a duration dictated by its source, followed by a short immunity to the Status after which the target can be frozen again.

Freezes have both a variable duration, and a variable immunity based on the source of the effect. For example, [[Ice spells]] have a duration dependent on the tier of spell used, starting at 8 ticks when using [[Ice Rush]] and increasing by 8<ref>Without the Ancient sceptre - See [[Freeze#Equipment|the equipment section]] for more information.</ref> for every tier of spell, with a freeze from [[Ice Barrage]] lasting up to 32 ticks (19.2 seconds). The immunity window for most freezes (with the exception of Grasp spells) is {{ticks|5}}. For Grasp spells it is only {{ticks|2}}.

Freeze only restricts regular movement, but not forced movement such as caused by [[Mithril seeds]] and [[Adamant seeds]] or by interacting with adjacent game objects such as ladders or cave entrances.

In [[PvP]], all freeze effects applied to other players will only restrict movement whilst both players remain within the 10-tile maximum player weapon range. Moving outside of this range will cause the frozen target to become free to move. The game code only checks the X and Y coordinates of both players, meaning a player who changes plane by e.g. going up a ladder will be able to maintain a freeze as long as they stay within the X and Y coordinate of their target.
