== Sources ==
===Weapons===
====Abyssal tentacle====
The [[Abyssal tentacle]] has a special attack, ''Binding Tentacle'', which freezes a target for {{ticks|8}} ''regardless'' of whether it landed a [[successful hit]].

====Zamorak godsword====
The [[Zamorak godsword]] has a special attack, ''Ice Cleave'', which freezes a target for {{ticks|32}} '''provided''' that it lands a successful hit.

===Spells===
Freezes are available on three different [[Spellbook|spellbooks]] with each type serving a different purpose. The only spellbook without any Freeze capability is the [[Lunar spellbook]].

The following tables will list durations in [[Game tick|ticks]], where each tick is equal to 0.6 seconds of real time. To learn more about ticks please refer to the [[Game tick]] page.

====Curse spells====
There are three [[Curse spells]] on the [[Standard spellbook]] which can apply Freeze. These spells do little or no damage, have no requirements other than Magic level, and the first two can be used by [[free-to-play]] players.

When a Bind-type spell is about to expire the chat box will report: {{Mes|The holding effect is beginning to fade.|color=red}} 

There is no message upon the spell being applied.

[[Blighted entangle sack]]s allow players to cast these spells in lieu of using runes while in the [[Wilderness]].

