==Equipment==
Certain [[Worn Equipment|equipment]] can increase the duration of, or otherwise synergise with specific sources of Freeze.

====Swampbark armour====
The [[Swampbark helm|helm]], [[Swampbark body|body]] and [[Swampbark legs|legs]] of [[Swampbark armour]] each increase the duration of freezing [[Curse spells]] from the [[Standard spellbook]] by 2 ticks, up to 6 ticks provided that all 3 aforementioned pieces are equipped. The gloves and boots do not provide any additional effect.

====Blue Moon armour====
Wearing the full [[Blue Moon armour]] set, the player gains the ''Frostweaver'' set effect, where after casting a Freeze spell the [[Blue Moon spear]] has a 20% chance for its next melee attack to be unaffected by attack delay. This chance increases to 50% when using the [[Arceuus spellbook]] [[Grasp spells]].

====Tome of Water====
The accuracy of all [[Curse spells]] from the [[Standard spellbook]], including the ones capable of freezing, is increased by 20% when wielding a charged [[tome of water]].

====Ancient sceptre====
The passive effect of an [[Ancient sceptre]] will increase the freeze duration of [[Ice spells]] by 10% while equipped by the player.

====Ice ancient sceptre====
The [[Ice ancient sceptre]] passively grants a 10% accuracy bonus to [[Ice spells]] on targets that can be frozen and are not currently frozen on top of the Ancient sceptre's base 10% duration increase.

==Trivia==
*The official name of this status effect per [[Monster Examine]] is ''Freeze'', however other popular community names include ''[[Bind]]'' or ''[[Entangle]]'' after the spells of the same name (the former being the first spell of this type available, and the latter having been the best spell of its type until the release of [[Ice spells]] along with [[Desert Treasure I|Desert Treasure]]) and ''Root'', a loanword from other games with a similar immobilising mechanic.

